 "findings": {
  "low_level": [
   "Throughput kernel at N 128 k 32: 528 SASS instructions for two rows against the control's 336 for one (IMAD 51 against the first batch's 128: the ternary exchange form removed the predicated moves, T53), 82 SHFL, 153 HMNMX2, 8 HSET2, 8 VOTE and 14 POPC for the tie class ballots. Registers 32 at N 32, 40 at N 64, 48 at N 128, 64 at N 256 (occupancy 8, 6, 5, 4 blocks per SM), the select-form kernel of the first batch had 29 to 48 at occupancy 8 to 5.",
   "The exact tie emission per packed word: two VOTE.ANY (one per row), four POPC (rank below the lane and total), two IADD, two ISETP against k and two predicated STS, about 10 instructions more than the scan-only emission of the fast form, 4 to 8 percent of the kernel from N 128 on."
  ],
  "algorithmic": [
   "Same-session throughput against the T42 one-word network (b2, both requirements identical): N 32 395 against 270 (1.46x), N 64 407 against 328 to 331 (1.23x to 1.24x), N 128 k 4 to 32 458 against 356 to 358 (1.28x to 1.29x), N 128 k 64 406 against 302 (1.34x), N 256 k 4 to 32 477 against 363 to 367 (1.30x to 1.32x), N 256 k 64 417 against 248 (1.68x). The first batch's select-form exchange measured 358, 418, 445, 405, 457, 409 at the same cells (control 270 to 367).",
   "Latency per call (two rows): 774 against 512 at N 32, 941 against 695 at N 64, 1352 against 1017 at N 128 k 32, 2353 against 1718 at N 256 k 32, 2138 against 1322 at N 256 k 64, that is 0.62x to 0.75x per call and 1.2x to 1.5x per row.",
   "The exact form is the right one where the tie class is large and must be index ordered in every call (quantized or relu logits with many equal keys at rank k), where the fast form's uniform fallback would run every call and cost its branch on top."
  ],
  "negative": [
   "Against the fast-recovery form (N5_rows_f, same session) the exact form is 4 to 8 percent slower from N 128 on (458 against 477 at N 128 k 32, 477 against 511 at N 256 k 32, 417 against 452 at N 256 k 64) and equal below.",
   "The select-form exchange of the first batch (three instructions per stage word) cost 3 percent against this card's ternary form at N 128 to 256 and gained 16 registers of occupancy back, which did not matter (T47 pipe bound)."
  ],
  "surprises": [
   "The ternary exchange form raised the throughput kernel's registers from 32 to 48 at N 128 and from 40 to 64 at N 256 (one fewer blocks per SM each) and still measured faster."
  ],
  "open_questions": [
   "Whether the two tie-class ballots per word can be issued back to back for all words (T52 notes the two-class pass does not reach the pipelined-ballot cost), not tried."
  ]
 },
