  "notes": "verify-N5 rerun 2026-10-25 on the card's node umbriel-b200-018 (B200, nvcc 13.4.92, container 6167d8b718ce as in the card), lease holder verify-N5, rebuilt from a git archive of exp/topk-swarm/N5 at the card's commit 30f5b8f821 (harness 0.5, SOURCE_COMMIT written, run.py --source-commit 30f5b8f821), built and measured under one lease, a separate source tree from the 8f613a317f cards. Batch state/results/verify-N5/N5_rows_vs_W1x_vimnmx_eager_focus_vG_20261025_163127.json (N 128, 256 x k 4, 16, 32, 64, both requirements, both regimes, one lock section, canaries 32.00098 cycles per op at both ends and 3779.8 and 3780.8 us). 32 of the card's 52 cells rerun (N 32 and 64 not rerun), all matched: every latency cell identical to the cycle, every throughput cell within 0.1 percent. Headline cells (rerun against card, control W1x_vimnmx_eager in the same lock section): N 128 k 32 458.2 against 458.3 with 358.2 against 358.2 (1.28x), N 256 k 64 417.0 against 416.8 with 248.4 against 248.4 (1.68x). Random cells N 128 k 16 458.3 against 458.3 and N 128 k 4 459.0 against 459.0 with 356.5. Latency two rows against one row 1352 against 1017 at N 128 k 32 and 2138 against 1322 at N 256 k 64 (1.33x to 1.62x per call). Both requirements measure the same to 0.1 percent and compile the same kernel (528 instructions at N 128 k 32 in both), as the card says. Control named, same lock section, control_is_aa false. Oracle 13 of 13 on variant and control in every cell, self test true, both rows checked per input (the per-row oracle is live, see the row 1 duplicate probe in the N5_rows_f verification). Throughput counts 2 N elements per call, the variant reaches at most 0.07 of the no-op ceiling. Resources: 0 bytes stack frame, 0 bytes spill, no STL and no LDL in any kernel built, registers as the card lists. SASS of the N 128 k 32 throughput kernel matches the low_level finding: 528 instructions, 82 SHFL, 153 HMNMX2 (predicated pairs), 8 HSET2, 8 VOTE, 14 POPC, 16 STS, control 336 with 75 SHFL and 153 VIMNMX. Exact recovery read in n5_detail.cuh: greater keys by the lane scan, equal keys ranked per word and per half by one ballot each in (word, lane) order, which is the index order of packed_rows, so prefer_smaller_index is exact by construction and the same code serves both requirements. Note on the commit: at 30f5b8f821 the fast-recovery adapters (N5_rows_f, N5_split_f, not this card) still took their tie-class fallback on a per-lane condition, the hardware-warp-uniform any-vote came in 8f613a317f, which does not touch this exact-form card and is uniform at warp scope anyway, but the b2 fast-form numbers quoted in the N5 findings were built with the per-lane form. Same node as the card, no cross-node measurement, small kernels. Verified."
